From 69d55141066a02314f723a39589c9fceae03610e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:49:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): stock page shows stock only; theme gets its own
 ribbon button
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Stock page drew the Machine, Post and Theme sections under the
stock controls, though Machine and Post have their own setup nodes
since #343/#390 and the theme is document-wide. The page now ends at
its action row; Machine and Post stay editable on their setup nodes.

The theme moved to a new "Theme…" ribbon door right of Panels (View
group). Its dropdown (theme_drop.rs, the View/machine door popup law)
lists Dark, Light, the discovered assets/themes/*.json files by name
and Browse..., then the colour-vision modes that rode inside the old
theme section. Picks queue SelectTheme / SelectThemeDialog /
SelectColorVision, so undo and redo hold. The unused colour-vision
combo is removed. Shell snapshots regenerated: only the ribbon moved.

Fixes #441

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
